# Tuff Design System (TDS)

Tuff Design System (TDS) is the shared visual contract across CoreApp, Nexus, TuffEx, AIUI (OpenUI), and the sandboxed Design Canvas. Every palette, surface material, motion rule, and primitive list resolves from one machine-checked catalog rather than hand-copied style tables.

## Single Source of Truth

All semantic design tokens live in `docs/design/tds/tokens.json` and govern three aligned token layers:

| Layer | Prefix | Scope | Authority |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| CoreApp Shell | `--shell-*` | Desktop chrome, workspace panes, canvas host | `apps/core-app/src/renderer/src/styles/shell-tokens.scss` |
| TuffEx Components | `--tx-*` | Vue 3 / Web Component / React primitives | `packages/tuffex/packages/components/style/variables.scss` |
| AI Suite (BUI) | `--tx-bui-*` | AI chat, reasoning, and agent surfaces | `packages/tuffex/packages/components/style/bui-tokens.scss` |

- `scripts/tds-tokens-sync.mjs` (`pnpm tds:check`) verifies zero drift across `tokens.json`, `shell-tokens.scss`, `variables.scss`, `bui-tokens.scss`, `TxBaseSurface.vue`, all 36 Core primitive directories, and all 51 WCAG 2.1 contrast pairs.
- Product pages consume `--shell-*` or `--tx-*` tokens only; raw hex/rgba literals and custom page override stylesheets are disallowed.

## Neutral Dark Base & Refraction Material

TDS pairs a calibrated neutral dark palette with physical glass refraction as its default surface material:

- **`#141414` dark canvas, never `#000000`**: Pure black triggers OLED purple smearing and flattens cast shadows. CoreApp and TuffEx converge on `#141414` for L0 canvas, `#1c1c1e` / `#1d1e1f` for L1 containers, and `#2c2c2e` / `#262727` for L2 elevated states.
- **`refraction` is the default surface**: `TxBaseSurface`, `TxCard`, `TxModal`, `TxPopover`, `TxSelect`, and `TxDropdownMenu` default to `mode="refraction"` (`refractionRenderer="css"`). Switching a surface to `flat`, `plain`, `mask`, `blur`, `glass`, `acrylic`, or `mica` requires explicit user confirmation.
- **Asymmetric motion degradation**: While dragging or resizing a transparent window, surfaces step down in **0ms** and recover after **140ms** of quiet so 120Hz frames stay smooth.
- **0.85 glass readability**: Translucent surfaces must maintain WCAG 2.1 AA readability when composited at `0.85` opacity over both light (`#e8e8ec`) and dark (`#0b0b0d`) desktop backdrops.

## 13–14px Productivity Typography & Instant Motion

Desktop tools optimize for rapid scanning density and immediate pointer feedback:

- **13–14px baseline**: Body copy is `13px`, input values are `14px`, secondary metadata is `12px`, captions are `11px`, and inline code scales optically to `0.9em` monospace.
- **Typography invariants**: Zero `letter-spacing` on body text, never `font-weight: 700` on prose, `text-wrap: balance` on headings, `text-wrap: pretty` on finalized prose, and `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums` for live metrics.
- **Dark optical weight compensation**: Emphasis weights step down by 40 in dark mode (`500 → 460`, `600 → 560`, `700 → 660`) to offset retinal irradiation.
- **Instant hover & phase-locked cadence**: Hover color shifts run at **0ms** with no color transition. Menu activation uses a `90ms + 90ms` confirmation rhythm, and persistent ambient indicators synchronize onto the 90ms `live-animation-clock` with reduced-motion and hidden-tab gating.

## Strict WCAG 2.1 AA/AAA Contrast Ramps

TDS ships four verified ramps (`:root`, `.dark`, `html.contrast`, `html.dark.contrast`) validated via real sRGB relative luminance and Porter-Duff alpha compositing:

- **Normal text**: `>= 4.5:1` (WCAG 2.1 AA), including semantic status chips measured against their composited `-soft` fill over `--shell-bg`.
- **High-contrast modes**: `html.contrast` and `html.dark.contrast` elevate body text to `>= 7.0:1` (AAA), disable translucent refraction, and re-bind shell semantics directly to `--tx-color-*` high-contrast mixins.
- **Triple-interlocked status**: Color never conveys state alone; status cues combine hue, icon glyph, and explicit text label.

## 3-Layer Declarative Theme Packs

`TdsThemePack` (`schemaVersion: 1`) is a strict pure-data JSON format shared between CoreApp desktop theming and the sandboxed Design Canvas:

1. **`tokens`**: Allowlisted `--shell-*` color ramp (light and dark) plus radius tokens; rejects `url()`, `javascript:`, `@import`, and raw CSS injection characters.
2. **`material`**: Window surface preference (`pure`, `refraction`, `filter`), motion tier (`full`, `crisp`, `reduced`), and clock cadence.
3. **`surface`**: Canvas backdrop pattern (`none`, `dots`, `grid`, `paper-grain`), accent tint opacity, and corner highlight.

Four built-in packs (`tds-apple-neutral`, `tds-obsidian-cobalt`, `tds-paper-ink`, `tds-graphite-emerald`) pass opaque and `0.85` refraction WCAG AA gates. Runtime styles scope to `:not(.contrast)` so custom packs never override accessibility high-contrast palettes.

## Core 36 Orthogonal Primitives

TuffEx exports 193 component modules, but everyday product screens and AI UI generation converge on **36 orthogonal Core primitives** across seven categories (Surface & Layout, Display, Data, Form & Input, Navigation, Overlay & Feedback, and AI Core):

- Eliminates synonym drift (for example choosing one canonical `TxSelect`, `TxModal`, and `TxEmptyState`).
- Keeps OpenUI schemas and LLM design prompts compact and deterministic, reducing hallucinated props and visual inconsistency.
- Specialized modules (`TxSensitiveInput`, `TxContextMenu`, `charts`, etc.) remain available via explicit upgrade paths when a screen exceeds the 36 Core primitives.

